WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:06.920
Speaker 1: The United States has now officially
said we do not believe that the recent surveillance

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:13.299
balloons slash devices tentatively believed
to be from China are evidence of intelligent

00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:20.500
aliens from another planet, solar system or
galaxy even visiting us on Earth.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:26.090
Joe Biden's press secretary, Karine Jean-Pierre,
making that statement during a press briefing

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:27.090
yesterday.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.410
Speaker 2: We addressed this from the White
House.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:34.410
I know there have been questions and concerns
about this, but there is no, again, no indication

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:39.100
of aliens or extraterrestrial activity with
these recent takedowns.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.989
Again, there is no indication of aliens or
terrestrial actors.

00:00:42.989 --> 00:00:46.879
Speaker 1: It's funny because the press corps
laughs.

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:48.469
But just look online.

00:00:48.469 --> 00:00:55.290
There are endless gobs of people convinced
that this is a cover up of extraterrestrial

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:56.290
encounters.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:01:00.239
Speaker 2: But with these recent takedowns,
we wanted to make sure that the American people

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:01.239
knew that.

00:01:01.239 --> 00:01:02.250
All of you knew that.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.809
And it was important for us to say that from
here, because we.

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:08.070
Speaker 1: Sure careen That's just what you
would say if you wanted to cover it up.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:09.310
Speaker 2: Hearing a lot about it.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:10.310
I'm not.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:11.310
Speaker 3: Jealous.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:18.640
Speaker 2: I'm just, you know, I loved E.T.,
the movie, but I'm going I'm just going to

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:19.640
leave it there.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:20.640
Speaker 1: All right.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.150
The National Security Council's John Kirby
also reiterated this and said this.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.220
These are not aliens.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.220
It's not aliens, folks.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:32.600
Speaker 3: The top officials in the Pentagon,
when asked explicitly if they were ruling

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:36.220
out any kind of extraterrestrial presence,
that they weren't doing anything out.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:41.890
And yet at the beginning of today's briefing,
albeit with her usual winning smile, Ms..

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:44.530
Jean-Pierre seemed to rule out any extraterrestrial
activity.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:48.940
Speaker 2: I don't think the American people
need to worry about aliens with respect to

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:49.940
these craft.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:50.940
Period.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:51.940
Speaker 1: I don't think there's any.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.780
Now, you heard what he said, right?

00:01:53.780 --> 00:02:01.630
I don't think the American people need to
worry about aliens with respect to these craft.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:07.119
And there are those who believe that Kirby
is very narrowly answering this question and

00:02:07.119 --> 00:02:11.630
saying these are not extraterrestrial aliens.

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:13.680
But that doesn't mean that there aren't others.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.010
Now, let's talk a little bit about aliens.

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:17.620
This is this is a very interesting topic.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:21.850
I want to expand on what I said during my
recent appearance with Anthony Pompliano when

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:23.500
I was down in Florida.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:27.590
One of the appearances I did was with Anthony
Pompliano, and he asked me about aliens.

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:32.019
It is really important to understand the sheer
vastness of the universe.

00:02:32.019 --> 00:02:36.260
You've got our galaxy, the Milky Way, hundreds
of billions of stars, and then all of the

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:38.640
accompanying planets and so on and so forth.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:46.291
So I do have a very general view that based
on what we know about the vastness of the

00:02:46.291 --> 00:02:53.310
universe, statistically, I think the likelihood
of extraterrestrial life of some kind could

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.360
be bacterial, could be intelligence.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.730
I don't know.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.500
I think the odds are high.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:04.900
The probability of that intelligent life having
already visited Earth, I believe, is extraordinarily

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:05.900
low.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.370
And the sort of math of it is as follows.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:11.370
You look at the number of stars in the universe,
it's astronomical.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:14.290
100 billion in our own Milky Way alone.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:19.830
With that number of stars, it is likely that
at least some planets would be capable of

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:21.420
supporting life.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:26.560
So the conditions, at least theoretically
for life, are probably not that rare.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:32.310
If you look at all of the planets that there
are, you then say, okay, well, on some fraction

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:38.069
of those that could support life, it doesn't
seem super unlikely, even if it's a small

00:03:38.069 --> 00:03:40.819
percentage that life would develop.

00:03:40.819 --> 00:03:47.390
And so I do think that when you consider all
of that and the age of the universe, 13.8

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:52.900
billion years old, that's a lot of time for
life to have evolved on other planets as well.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:58.049
So I think it is likely, given the laws of
physics and chemistry, which appear to be

00:03:58.049 --> 00:04:03.470
universal and all these different things,
it's likely that there is life on other planets.

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:10.879
Do I think it has reached Earth in the form
of a balloon or a cylinder or, you know, humanoid

00:04:10.879 --> 00:04:14.730
four foot tall aliens with obsessed with anal
probes?

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:17.470
It must be proctology, must be big on other
planets.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:21.290
I don't know that I don't have any evidence
for.

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:26.759
And then when you look at the numerous so-called
UFO sightings over the years, we have a lack

00:04:26.759 --> 00:04:28.180
of concrete evidence.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:33.250
We see that the stories that are told match
the images of supposed aliens from movies

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:38.430
and from popular culture, and many are specifically
debunked as aircraft or weather balloon or

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:39.430
birds or whatever.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:42.449
So, you know, there's that there's the lack
of physical evidence in all of these different

00:04:42.449 --> 00:04:43.449
things.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:50.550
So really funny coda to this, which is Mark
Esper, Trump's former secretary of defense,

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:56.370
who says, you know, if aliens were to come
here, I don't think this is exactly what they

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.370
would do.

00:04:57.370 --> 00:04:58.370
Careful.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:02.020
Speaker 4: I'm confident saying that I doubt
that the aliens would travel across the universe

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:06.630
and all of a sudden decide to conduct surveillance
over Lake Huron in a balloon moving 20 miles

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:07.630
per hour.

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:11.340
That's a plan that I think we're in good shape
and we now know we can shoot them down.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:12.930
But I don't think that's true at all.

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:18.760
Look, my hunch is that these are weather balloons
or scientific experiments put off by another

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:22.080
country, another company or some nonprofit.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.669
We'll learn that in due course.

00:05:23.669 --> 00:05:26.850
Speaker 1: Yeah, I you know, I it makes sense.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:31.710
Esper is not a guy that I found super interesting
as an elected official or whatever, But I

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:32.860
do think this is a good point.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:39.080
And it's similar to, you know, if if the aliens
really were making contact, I don't know that

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:42.690
their priority would necessarily be anal probes.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:46.610
And so it's sort of weird that that's a big
part of a lot of the stories that are.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:51.930
I think Esper is right, but maybe that's just
what the aliens want us to think.

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:56.790
It's not us because we would never just go
20 miles an hour over one of the Great Lakes.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:57.950
Let me know what you think.

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:02.210
I agree with Karine Jean-Pierre and Kirby
and Esper.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.919
I do not believe this is evidence of alien
contact.

